    "If one day you want your own map, do not look for a sign on the door. Look for the smell of ink and old wood, a narrow corridor, a doorbell slow to ring. And bring in memory a whole day of waiting — not to punish yourself, but to finally see the outline of what you inhabited.",
    "Inês never married the craft or the silence. She learned to dine with friends, to travel without measuring minutes, to stand in line when necessary without feeling life slip away. The atlas of lost hours kept growing — not as an archive of defeats, but as an atlas of human places where one can still sit until the next chapter begins.",
